Package: rsagePath
Title: Path Analysis and Exploratory Causal Graph Module for R Sage
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("R Sage contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "noreply@rsage.dev")
Description: Path analysis for several observed variables, aimed at small
    samples where the covariates and the routes between variables are not
    known in advance. Variables are placed in ordered tiers (background,
    early, middle, outcome); arrows only run forward. The structure is
    learned from the data with 'bnlearn' bootstrap model averaging under the
    tier order, taken as every forward path (saturated), or given as a path
    list. The model is estimated with 'lavaan' (ML with bootstrap or Monte
    Carlo intervals, FIML for missing data) or 'blavaan' (Bayesian), drawn
    with 'tidySEM', split into direct, path-specific indirect and total
    effects, and used to sort the other variables into confounders,
    mediators and colliders with 'dagitty' adjustment sets.
    analyse() returns an 'rsage' result that prints in the console and
    renders in Quarto documents.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: rsage (>= 0.1.0), lavaan, ggplot2, stats, utils
Suggests: bnlearn, dagitty, tidySEM, blavaan, lavaanExtra, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
